                <pb facs="0762" n="754" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg754"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363 Amiranian/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-29T11:00:00+03:25">May 29, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>56. My 49, May 21, 3 p.m. I am informed Hart who is now in Kabul has decided to
                    postpone notification to the Afghan Government until June 4 and formal written
                    notification here until June 6. I also hear that Clapp intends to apply for oil
                    concession in southeastern Iran. It is difficult to reconcile these maneuvers
                    with the <pb facs="0763" n="755" xml:id="pg755"/> company’s decision and they
                    may have a deplorable effect upon a situation which is already bad enough.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
